    "information": {
      "description": "<p><em>Built early in the 4th Corporate War to fix the Standard-B's worst habit, which was losing open fights. Arasaka chased speed, reflexes and control, and hung a suit-sized sword on the back for anything that got close. It ran rings around slower Militech suits. As far as anyone will admit, the line ended decades ago, so every one still walking has a story.</em></p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> 42,324eb (Super Luxury)<br><strong>Frame / Shell:</strong> Beta / Hybrid Metalgear®<br><strong>Stats:</strong> 30 HP • 16 SP • BODY 14 • +1 MOVE<br><strong>Onboard weapons:</strong> Arasaka RAS-16 Ieyasu, TUp (5d6 Damage) Arasaka Murasame Katana, Pursuit Security Crybaby, Techtronika BMG-570 (Silver), Tsunami Arms Kasha<br><strong>Onboard cyberware:</strong> Kerenzikov, Reflex Co-Processor, Low Light/Infrared/UV, Targeting Scope, Skate Foot</p><p>One pilot. The suit's stats modify the pilot's; see the Item Compendium, Power Armor.</p><p><small>Item Compendium (2070) • Power Armor</small></p>",
